WEBVTT

00:06.673 --> 00:08.675
[theme music playing]

00:29.070 --> 00:30.196
[line ringing]

00:41.875 --> 00:46.963
WHEN THE PHONE RINGS

01:03.021 --> 01:04.189
[somber music playing]

01:29.881 --> 01:30.965
- [gasps]
- [music ends]

01:33.092 --> 01:34.093
[breath trembling]

01:42.352 --> 01:43.228
[sighs]

01:45.355 --> 01:46.189
[groans]

01:47.357 --> 01:48.274
[Sa-eon groans softly]

02:06.126 --> 02:08.128
[soft music playing]

02:32.694 --> 02:33.695
[Sa-eon groans]

02:34.612 --> 02:35.697
[Sa-eon breathing heavily]

02:46.374 --> 02:47.417
[breathing heavily]

02:48.543 --> 02:49.544
What happened?

02:53.631 --> 02:55.216
[footsteps echoing]

02:58.428 --> 03:00.513
- What happened next?
- [water running]

03:04.434 --> 03:05.393
[breath trembling]

03:06.019 --> 03:07.437
[Do-jae] Can you guess who it is?

03:08.104 --> 03:09.772
Someone who's close to you

03:10.523 --> 03:12.442
and knows you…

03:12.525 --> 03:13.860
[tense music playing]

03:14.694 --> 03:15.612
[sighs]

03:15.695 --> 03:18.698
[Do-jae] The waveform analysis indicates
a woman in her twenties.

03:22.994 --> 03:24.787
[Sa-eon] Compare it with 406.

03:24.871 --> 03:26.789
See how much they match in percentage.

03:26.873 --> 03:28.124
Up to two decimal places.

03:30.293 --> 03:31.294
[knocking on door]

03:32.670 --> 03:34.631
EPISODE 6

04:02.617 --> 04:03.451
[Sa-eon] Why…

04:04.953 --> 04:07.956
were we lying on the floor together
last night?

04:12.252 --> 04:14.295
What? What is it?

04:20.093 --> 04:20.927
[scoffs]

04:21.886 --> 04:23.096
What is it?

04:23.721 --> 04:26.474
Tell me if something happened.

04:36.651 --> 04:38.695
[Hee-joo] Should I tell you
everything honestly?

04:40.613 --> 04:41.447
Honest…

04:42.532 --> 04:44.367
"Tell you everything honestly"?

04:44.450 --> 04:46.452
[quirky music playing]

05:13.479 --> 05:14.605
[phone ringing]

05:22.113 --> 05:23.114
[door opens]

05:23.197 --> 05:24.490
PARK DO-JAE

05:28.036 --> 05:28.870
Yes?

05:28.953 --> 05:29.787
Mr. Paik.

05:30.580 --> 05:31.622
What happened?

05:31.706 --> 05:33.541
Your phone was off. I was worried.

05:33.624 --> 05:34.542
[sighs softly]

05:34.625 --> 05:35.918
I'm sorry.

05:36.002 --> 05:37.003
It just happened.

05:37.754 --> 05:39.589
As for the favor I asked for yesterday?

05:39.672 --> 05:40.840
Did you not see it?

05:41.632 --> 05:43.342
I sent you a text last night.

05:43.968 --> 05:45.219
But you never responded.

05:52.852 --> 05:54.395
[solemn music playing]

05:54.896 --> 05:55.855
[sighs softly]

06:02.070 --> 06:06.657
[Do-jae] It's a 99.99% match.

06:10.787 --> 06:12.955
I made a summary of all the events so far.

06:13.039 --> 06:14.791
From the first threatening call

06:14.874 --> 06:17.543
to the recent incident
at the nursing home.

06:17.627 --> 06:18.878
I came to one conclusion.

06:18.961 --> 06:20.671
The caller, 406, isn't involved

06:20.755 --> 06:23.591
in the kidnapping, explosion,
and nursing home incident.

06:23.674 --> 06:24.634
There's someone else.

06:26.427 --> 06:27.678
I know that.

06:28.387 --> 06:29.722
They're not accomplices.

06:31.766 --> 06:34.936
You have an idea who 406 might be,
don't you?

06:35.019 --> 06:36.187
I'm sorry.

06:36.938 --> 06:38.648
I can't tell you right now.

06:39.315 --> 06:43.653
For now, let's find the connection
between him and 406 and break it.

06:45.113 --> 06:46.114
After that…

06:47.907 --> 06:49.033
[Do-jae] Are you okay?

06:50.076 --> 06:51.077
You don't look well.

06:53.496 --> 06:54.497
I'm fine.

06:57.125 --> 06:58.042
Yes, sir.

06:58.960 --> 07:00.211
If you need anything--

07:00.294 --> 07:01.337
[Sa-eon] No.

07:02.839 --> 07:03.923
I'm not okay.

07:05.591 --> 07:06.717
[scoffs]

07:06.801 --> 07:08.928
[dramatic music playing]

07:09.595 --> 07:10.888
You see,

07:12.431 --> 07:15.351
I thought
I'd controlled situations perfectly

07:15.435 --> 07:17.520
and made better judgments than anyone.

07:18.604 --> 07:20.857
I thought I had lived meticulously

07:22.567 --> 07:25.069
not to fall into any traps.

07:29.323 --> 07:30.450
But…

07:31.242 --> 07:32.577
why didn't I know?

07:32.660 --> 07:33.786
[scoffs]

07:33.870 --> 07:34.787
When I think back,

07:35.621 --> 07:37.623
there were more than a few hints.

07:39.375 --> 07:42.462
Maybe I just ignored them.

07:43.337 --> 07:45.756
I firmly believed it couldn't be true,

07:45.840 --> 07:48.176
desperately hoping it wasn't.

07:49.552 --> 07:51.137
But I shouldn't have done that.

07:51.971 --> 07:54.098
I should've at least prepared myself.

07:54.974 --> 07:56.225
If I had,

07:56.309 --> 07:59.729
I wouldn't be at a loss for what to do.

08:02.690 --> 08:04.525
You have until tomorrow to decide.

08:05.276 --> 08:07.278
Or we can settle for two billion won.

08:07.361 --> 08:08.529
You have until tomorrow.

08:08.613 --> 08:10.656
It's not like you married her for love.

08:10.740 --> 08:12.283
You don't even love her now.

08:12.366 --> 08:14.118
If it's going to be like that,

08:15.912 --> 08:17.538
just leave her.

08:24.754 --> 08:25.588
THE SEVENTH CALL

08:25.671 --> 08:28.382
Then why did you treat her
like she was invisible?

08:28.966 --> 08:29.842
[scoffs]

08:32.553 --> 08:33.387
[sighs deeply]

08:38.142 --> 08:39.477
THE THIRD CALL

08:39.560 --> 08:40.811
It's Hong Hee-joo's…

08:40.895 --> 08:42.355
[dramatic music playing]

08:45.733 --> 08:46.984
[softly] …thigh.

08:52.114 --> 08:53.908
You're supposed to be her husband.

08:54.825 --> 08:57.662
Didn't you know
Hee-joo has a unique mole on her thigh?

08:58.412 --> 09:00.331
How could you not know?

09:00.915 --> 09:03.000
Were you just not interested, or…

09:04.961 --> 09:06.462
have you never seen her naked?

09:09.090 --> 09:10.091
[laughing]

09:13.761 --> 09:14.637
[bangs table]

09:15.263 --> 09:16.097
Enough.

09:18.140 --> 09:19.308
[sighs in exasperation]

09:21.435 --> 09:22.979
[slow music playing]

09:23.062 --> 09:24.063
[chuckles frustratingly]

09:33.781 --> 09:34.699
[exhales nervously]

09:55.845 --> 09:57.054
It grew longer as I wrote.

09:58.639 --> 10:00.433
100 QUESTIONS, 100 ANSWERS

10:03.978 --> 10:05.980
Wait. I forgot one.

10:11.402 --> 10:13.321
LIES, ANGER, HATRED,
MISUNDERSTANDING, FORGIVENESS

10:13.404 --> 10:14.780
What's the sign language

10:15.364 --> 10:16.282
for forgiveness?

10:24.874 --> 10:28.336
What about "I forgive your wrongdoings"?

10:35.426 --> 10:37.428
[solemn music playing]

10:57.365 --> 10:58.199
[sighs wearily]

10:59.033 --> 11:00.076
It's difficult.

11:01.202 --> 11:02.036
Forgiveness.

11:02.703 --> 11:04.288
[gripping music playing]

11:06.666 --> 11:08.250
Let's end today's class here.

11:29.397 --> 11:30.439
[phone vibrates]

11:36.779 --> 11:39.907
YOU DIDN'T TEXT BACK,
SO I'M TEXTING AGAIN. LET'S MEET UP TODAY.

11:50.709 --> 11:52.294
SIGN LANGUAGE

11:58.134 --> 12:01.887
[You-ri] The pre-candidate registration
for the 21st presidential election,

12:01.971 --> 12:05.141
which will be held in March next year,
will begin next week.

12:05.891 --> 12:07.309
Sir.

12:07.393 --> 12:10.146
It's about the task
you asked me to check regularly.

12:10.229 --> 12:14.150
Regarding Chairman Hong Il-gyeong's
eldest daughter, Hong In-a.

12:27.621 --> 12:29.623
[solemn music playing]

12:46.140 --> 12:47.141
[Ui-yong] Honey.

12:47.224 --> 12:50.227
Chairman Hong's eldest daughter
is back in Korea.

12:52.855 --> 12:53.939
So what?

12:54.023 --> 12:56.108
What do you mean?

12:56.192 --> 12:58.235
You should meet with her.

12:58.319 --> 13:00.738
And ask her why she caused that mess.

13:00.821 --> 13:03.657
No, before that, see if we can control…

13:04.909 --> 13:05.993
Are you drinking?

13:08.162 --> 13:09.246
Are you drunk?

13:11.749 --> 13:13.083
Can't I be drunk?

13:14.335 --> 13:15.586
On a day like today?

13:17.129 --> 13:18.088
What's today?

13:20.257 --> 13:21.091
What is it?

13:25.971 --> 13:27.306
A day no one can remember.

13:28.474 --> 13:31.435
A day that shouldn't be remembered.

13:32.186 --> 13:35.022
That's what your father decided.

13:35.105 --> 13:36.106
So what?

13:38.150 --> 13:41.654
Why? Must you pretend to care?

13:42.238 --> 13:44.823
Would that ease your guilt a little?

13:45.699 --> 13:46.867
Don't make me laugh.

13:47.576 --> 13:49.620
Twenty years ago today,

13:49.703 --> 13:52.540
both you and I know how we really felt!

13:55.793 --> 13:56.627
What?

13:59.797 --> 14:01.131
A sense of freedom.

14:01.215 --> 14:02.800
[somber music playing]

14:16.063 --> 14:17.481
[banging on door]

14:19.149 --> 14:21.569
- [banging continues]
- [boy crying]

14:28.951 --> 14:30.953
[somber music continues playing]

15:05.362 --> 15:07.740
IS IT IMPOSSIBLE
TO CHANGE INNATE TEMPERAMENT?

15:09.992 --> 15:11.994
[ethereal music playing]

15:42.900 --> 15:44.151
[Yeon-hui] Goodness.

15:44.234 --> 15:45.402
You must be In-a.

15:46.528 --> 15:48.489
How dare you touch me
with your filthy hands?

15:48.572 --> 15:49.573
[Yeon-hui huffs]

15:55.788 --> 15:57.790
[solemn music playing]

16:56.849 --> 16:57.975
Hee-joo.

17:03.313 --> 17:04.606
How have you been?

17:04.690 --> 17:06.692
[music intensifies]

17:08.694 --> 17:09.695
[music ends]

17:11.071 --> 17:12.072
[In-a] Do you remember?

17:12.740 --> 17:14.783
We'd visit the aquarium often as kids.

17:15.743 --> 17:18.912
It felt like all the sounds
in the world disappeared

17:20.456 --> 17:22.833
when I stared into the water like this.

17:23.792 --> 17:25.294
It made me feel at peace.

17:27.880 --> 17:29.465
Let's see the mermaid show you like.

17:30.049 --> 17:30.883
It starts soon.

17:32.426 --> 17:33.343
Isn't it amazing?

17:33.927 --> 17:35.721
Hearing me chattering like this.

17:36.430 --> 17:38.098
I must've been lucky.

17:38.182 --> 17:40.100
The surgery was a success.

17:40.184 --> 17:43.228
No surgery could fix me when I was young.

17:49.151 --> 17:50.486
But, Hee-joo…

17:52.946 --> 17:54.490
why are you still the same?

17:55.824 --> 17:57.367
You can talk now.

17:58.035 --> 17:59.620
You don't need to keep quiet.

18:08.212 --> 18:10.756
[Hee-joo] You knew?

18:11.548 --> 18:12.382
[In-a] Yeah.

18:14.510 --> 18:16.011
You didn't speak…

18:18.263 --> 18:19.640
because of me.

18:26.271 --> 18:28.023
[In-a panting]

18:29.358 --> 18:30.609
I know.

18:31.401 --> 18:33.278
I did a terrible thing to you.

18:33.904 --> 18:35.739
I know it was awful of me,

18:37.533 --> 18:39.409
but I didn't want to fall apart alone.

18:40.244 --> 18:42.037
I needed someone to be miserable

18:43.914 --> 18:44.998
with me.

18:48.252 --> 18:49.378
Hee-joo.

18:50.754 --> 18:51.672
So what?

18:51.755 --> 18:54.550
Now that you're okay,
are you allowing me to speak?

18:56.218 --> 18:57.928
No, that's not up to you.

18:59.012 --> 19:00.389
I'll decide it.

19:00.889 --> 19:02.808
I won't let you interfere
in my life anymore.

19:05.060 --> 19:06.895
You don't know what I'm saying, do you?

19:06.979 --> 19:08.147
It doesn't matter.

19:08.230 --> 19:10.732
I'll say what I want,
just like what you're doing.

19:14.903 --> 19:17.197
THE LITTLE MERMAID'S MYSTERIOUS ADVENTURE

19:17.281 --> 19:18.407
[scoffs]

19:20.242 --> 19:22.077
I don't like The Little Mermaid.

19:22.786 --> 19:23.620
I hate her.

19:23.704 --> 19:25.706
[somber music playing]

19:36.508 --> 19:37.509
[exhales heavily]

19:40.596 --> 19:41.597
[phone vibrating]

19:44.516 --> 19:46.185
IN-A

19:53.817 --> 19:54.818
[phone vibrates]

20:00.908 --> 20:01.742
[In-a] Hee-joo.

20:02.826 --> 20:05.287
I needed to tell you something today.

20:05.370 --> 20:08.707
Do you think you know Paik Sa-eon well?

20:14.254 --> 20:17.382
Before the wedding,
I didn't dump you on him.

20:17.466 --> 20:19.301
He asked for you.

20:19.384 --> 20:21.386
In return for letting me go,

20:21.929 --> 20:24.223
he needed a connection to our family,

20:24.306 --> 20:25.724
so he took you hostage.

20:33.982 --> 20:35.651
[Do-jae] I came to one conclusion.

20:36.235 --> 20:37.819
The caller, 406, isn't involved

20:37.903 --> 20:40.697
in the kidnapping, explosion,
and nursing home incident.

20:40.781 --> 20:41.740
There's someone else.

20:41.823 --> 20:43.825
[suspenseful music playing]

21:25.659 --> 21:27.661
[music slows down]

21:36.670 --> 21:37.921
[sighs]

21:46.805 --> 21:48.807
[suspenseful music resumes]

22:04.197 --> 22:05.115
It's just…

22:05.824 --> 22:07.743
My phone's missing.

22:08.410 --> 22:10.120
[Hee-joo] Why is he looking for that here?

22:13.457 --> 22:14.875
CALLS
PAIK SA-EON

22:14.958 --> 22:16.543
- [Sa-eon sighs]
- [phone ringing]

22:19.963 --> 22:21.006
[clears throat]

22:32.601 --> 22:33.435
Wait.

22:34.311 --> 22:35.145
What's this?

22:38.148 --> 22:39.066
[scoffs]

22:40.108 --> 22:41.276
So Hee-joo was…

22:42.861 --> 22:44.529
into this kind of thing?

22:50.744 --> 22:51.745
[Sa-eon grunts]

22:57.584 --> 22:58.919
[soft music playing]

23:27.864 --> 23:28.865
Did I…

23:30.867 --> 23:31.701
I mean,

23:32.953 --> 23:33.787
did we…

23:35.705 --> 23:36.540
by any chance…

23:42.921 --> 23:44.047
[footsteps receding]

23:44.131 --> 23:45.257
[door opens]

23:49.636 --> 23:50.637
[gasps]

23:54.266 --> 23:55.225
[sighs in relief]

24:02.649 --> 24:03.775
[door opens]

24:03.859 --> 24:04.860
[door closes]

24:19.040 --> 24:20.167
[sighs]

24:20.250 --> 24:22.169
I must be insane.

24:23.461 --> 24:24.629
[exhales heavily]

24:26.047 --> 24:26.965
[sighs]

24:34.055 --> 24:36.057
[breathing heavily]

24:39.477 --> 24:41.479
[panting]

24:48.612 --> 24:49.738
[phone vibrating]

24:57.204 --> 24:58.705
[line ringing]

25:00.248 --> 25:01.708
[Sa-eon over call] How did you know?

25:03.043 --> 25:04.002
About what?

25:04.085 --> 25:07.005
[Sa-eon] That I've been thinking about you
all day long.

25:07.964 --> 25:10.133
We spoke on the phone every day.

25:10.759 --> 25:14.262
But there are still so many things
I don't know about you.

25:16.473 --> 25:18.308
So now I want to know more.

25:19.392 --> 25:20.477
[Hee-joo] Then…

25:21.436 --> 25:24.606
how about we each
ask a question and answer?

25:24.689 --> 25:25.523
Sounds good.

25:26.191 --> 25:27.651
However, from this moment on,

25:28.526 --> 25:30.362
we'll only speak the truth.

25:31.071 --> 25:32.030
That's what I want.

25:33.615 --> 25:34.783
Go ahead.

25:35.700 --> 25:37.202
The day before the wedding,

25:37.911 --> 25:40.247
you said you met In-a and made a deal.

25:42.791 --> 25:45.126
Was the deal about Hong Hee-joo?

25:45.210 --> 25:46.044
[Sa-eon] Yes.

25:47.295 --> 25:48.213
It's my turn.

25:49.005 --> 25:51.591
What? My question isn't over yet.

25:51.675 --> 25:53.134
I answered, so it's over.

25:53.218 --> 25:55.637
Think carefully next time before you ask.

25:56.763 --> 25:57.973
It's my turn.

25:58.056 --> 26:01.810
Is Hong Hee-joo being threatened
right now?

26:03.061 --> 26:05.230
Why do you think she's being threatened?

26:05.313 --> 26:07.399
[Sa-eon] 406, you kidnapped Hee-joo

26:07.482 --> 26:09.317
and even attacked her father.

26:09.401 --> 26:11.069
You're completely insane.

26:13.238 --> 26:14.572
Hee-joo would never side

26:15.282 --> 26:16.741
with someone like you.

26:18.285 --> 26:21.788
She's being threatened but also not, okay?

26:22.831 --> 26:23.832
It's my turn now.

26:24.457 --> 26:26.251
Did you take Hong Hee-joo hostage

26:26.334 --> 26:29.504
in exchange for letting Hong In-a go free
from the arranged marriage?

26:31.589 --> 26:32.799
Who told you that?

26:33.383 --> 26:36.052
Seeing how you're asking that,
I guess it's true.

26:37.804 --> 26:38.638
It's true.

26:40.432 --> 26:41.349
I…

26:41.891 --> 26:43.935
often have nightmares.

26:44.602 --> 26:46.521
I had them more often as a kid.

26:54.237 --> 26:55.071
[gasps softly]

27:14.758 --> 27:15.884
[young Hee-joo] I will

27:16.718 --> 27:17.552
help you.

27:18.428 --> 27:21.139
I will be with you.

27:23.350 --> 27:24.893
It's okay.

27:25.894 --> 27:26.853
It's okay.

27:44.871 --> 27:45.705
It's okay.

27:48.958 --> 27:50.460
[breath trembling]

27:52.629 --> 27:53.588
It's okay.

27:53.671 --> 27:56.007
What calmed me down every time…

27:57.967 --> 27:59.886
were the gestures of the girl next door

28:01.638 --> 28:03.640
who practiced sign language every night.

28:06.101 --> 28:07.602
But that girl

28:09.020 --> 28:10.105
had no one

28:11.398 --> 28:13.066
to rely on, anywhere.

28:14.776 --> 28:16.194
Because to her,

28:17.821 --> 28:20.240
Chairman Hong's house was a prison.

28:22.075 --> 28:24.244
I wanted to help her escape.

28:25.120 --> 28:26.454
Hoping that she could

28:27.789 --> 28:29.707
leave that house and live freely.

28:31.584 --> 28:33.044
But I never imagined…

28:35.004 --> 28:36.089
that I would become

28:37.757 --> 28:39.259
Hee-joo's new prison.

28:40.260 --> 28:41.469
[Hee-joo] Prison?

28:43.054 --> 28:44.305
A married life with me

28:45.223 --> 28:47.058
after leaving that house

28:48.768 --> 28:51.438
must've felt like a prison to her.

28:52.397 --> 28:55.233
That must be why
she got mixed up with some crazy person

28:55.859 --> 28:58.027
in order to divorce me, right?

29:01.114 --> 29:02.365
It's my turn now.

29:04.451 --> 29:05.785
Does Hong Hee-joo

29:07.412 --> 29:08.830
still want a divorce?

29:14.753 --> 29:16.004
Answer me, 406.

29:16.755 --> 29:18.465
Isn't that what you kept saying?

29:18.548 --> 29:21.384
To let Hee-joo go
and return things to the way they were.

29:23.136 --> 29:24.387
To let go of her.

29:28.016 --> 29:30.310
She didn't want
to get her hopes up anymore.

29:31.478 --> 29:32.687
"Someday,

29:34.606 --> 29:35.857
things will change."

29:37.942 --> 29:41.696
"It'll get better."
She waited and hoped for three years.

29:42.489 --> 29:43.573
If you let her go,

29:44.699 --> 29:46.367
she thought she wouldn't get hurt

29:47.202 --> 29:49.996
or be disappointed anymore.

29:50.079 --> 29:52.373
That's what Hong Hee-joo thought.

29:52.457 --> 29:53.708
By any chance,

29:55.543 --> 29:56.836
does Hee-joo want…

30:00.423 --> 30:01.424
SINCERITY

30:01.508 --> 30:02.592
…sincerity,

30:04.010 --> 30:05.386
attention,

30:05.470 --> 30:06.679
understanding,

30:07.388 --> 30:08.306
and affection?

30:09.224 --> 30:10.391
Is that what she wants?

30:12.519 --> 30:14.479
What are you saying? What I'm saying--

30:14.562 --> 30:15.897
[Sa-eon] I can give that to her.

30:21.486 --> 30:22.904
I can give her everything.

30:26.241 --> 30:29.828
If that's what Hee-joo wants,
I'll give as much as she needs.

30:31.204 --> 30:33.039
Why do you suddenly want to do that?

30:35.750 --> 30:37.794
You didn't care whether I lived or died,

30:37.877 --> 30:40.129
or whether I was by your side, until now.

30:41.089 --> 30:42.090
From the very start…

30:44.926 --> 30:47.011
this wasn't a marriage Hee-joo wanted.

30:48.054 --> 30:50.265
I kept her by my side as a hostage,

30:52.183 --> 30:53.768
thinking that someday

30:54.769 --> 30:56.354
I'd have to let her go.

30:58.648 --> 31:00.650
Is that why you were so cruel?

31:01.860 --> 31:03.069
So you wouldn't get attached?

31:03.820 --> 31:05.405
But if that's what Hee-joo wants,

31:06.573 --> 31:07.574
it changes things.

31:10.493 --> 31:11.494
Then promise me.

31:12.620 --> 31:13.746
If I make an effort

31:15.248 --> 31:16.708
and we can change,

31:17.834 --> 31:20.795
promise you'll never make this call again.

31:26.926 --> 31:28.344
That depends on how you act.

31:28.428 --> 31:30.430
[intense music playing]

32:10.553 --> 32:12.180
- [Yeon-hui chuckles]
- Oh my, ma'am.

32:12.972 --> 32:15.558
You look so young and beautiful today.

32:15.642 --> 32:17.435
- [men laugh]
- [Yeon-hui] Of course.

32:17.518 --> 32:19.896
My age may increase,
but my skirt length shouldn't.

32:19.979 --> 32:21.856
Of course. [chuckles]

32:22.815 --> 32:24.734
Can't you dress a bit younger too?

32:26.486 --> 32:28.738
Why should I have to struggle
to look younger?

32:29.989 --> 32:32.575
[Il-gyeong laughing] You're right.

32:32.659 --> 32:34.285
It wouldn't suit you.

32:34.369 --> 32:37.038
You already have a gorgeous charm
about you.

32:37.121 --> 32:38.206
[Yeon-hui clears throat]

32:38.831 --> 32:40.333
[Ui-yong laughing]

32:40.416 --> 32:42.168
Okay, then.

32:42.710 --> 32:44.629
Get in. Good luck today.

32:44.712 --> 32:45.797
[Ui-yong laughs]

32:46.381 --> 32:47.715
Let's go. Okay.

32:58.059 --> 33:00.019
- [Il-gyeong applauding]
- [Ui-yong chuckles]

33:05.358 --> 33:07.026
How much is Spokesperson Paik asking for?

33:07.110 --> 33:07.944
What?

33:08.027 --> 33:09.487
What's his price?

33:10.071 --> 33:11.322
Good luck with the negotiation.

33:11.406 --> 33:12.865
Between parents and children,

33:13.408 --> 33:15.243
there should be
some playful give-and-take.

33:15.326 --> 33:16.160
I don't know.

33:17.328 --> 33:19.747
Don't you know as well as I do?

33:20.581 --> 33:22.667
Getting a stubborn child to listen

33:23.835 --> 33:26.337
- is harder than practicing discipline.
- [Il-gyeong chuckles]

33:26.421 --> 33:27.755
Your eldest daughter.

33:29.173 --> 33:30.675
Do you know how she's doing?

33:32.176 --> 33:34.470
Why would you suddenly bring her up?

33:35.680 --> 33:37.348
She comes to mind lately.

33:38.141 --> 33:41.144
I wonder how she's doing.

33:45.940 --> 33:47.025
[sighs]

33:48.484 --> 33:50.153
[Young-woo] Are you ready for this?

33:50.236 --> 33:51.863
[Won-bin] I've never been to a retreat.

33:51.946 --> 33:53.448
[Young-woo] I've organized this well.

33:53.531 --> 33:56.409
- [Won-bin] I am a little nervous.
- [woman] Is that your security pillow?

33:57.243 --> 33:59.954
[Young-woo] So only Mr. Paik and Mr. Park
aren't here yet?

34:00.038 --> 34:01.664
- Should I call them?
- Nah.

34:01.748 --> 34:03.916
What? What's that?

34:05.001 --> 34:06.127
[employee 1] What is that?

34:06.210 --> 34:07.628
THANK YOU, SPOKESPERSON'S TEAM

34:08.880 --> 34:10.214
WHEEL LUNCHBOX

34:11.007 --> 34:13.885
TO THE SPOKESPERSON'S TEAM, THANK YOU

34:14.552 --> 34:15.553
Let's go.

34:17.055 --> 34:19.057
[quirky music playing]

34:20.850 --> 34:22.852
The staff from the spokesperson's office?

34:22.935 --> 34:25.063
- [all] Yes.
- The lunchboxes have arrived.

34:28.441 --> 34:29.567
- Thank you.
- Here you go.

34:30.193 --> 34:31.360
Pass these out.

34:31.444 --> 34:32.653
Take that.

34:34.113 --> 34:35.073
Thank you.

34:36.032 --> 34:37.075
Goodness.

34:37.158 --> 34:38.493
[all gasping]

34:38.576 --> 34:41.120
- [Young-woo] Do you have mine?
- [employee 2] Goodness.

34:41.204 --> 34:42.497
[employee 2] Look at the hearts.

34:42.580 --> 34:45.917
[chuckles softly]
"An office full of love."

34:46.000 --> 34:47.877
Is that what this is, Mr. Kang?

34:47.960 --> 34:50.004
It wasn't me. I didn't order these.

34:50.088 --> 34:51.339
Who sent these?

34:52.173 --> 34:53.007
I don't know.

34:53.091 --> 34:54.092
[music fades]

34:54.717 --> 34:56.344
[Sa-eon] Is everyone here?

34:56.427 --> 34:58.513
[all] Hello.

35:01.182 --> 35:03.768
The lunchboxes came too.

35:03.851 --> 35:07.271
Wait, did you order these, sir?

35:09.023 --> 35:10.066
[sighs]

35:14.320 --> 35:17.115
- Let's go.
- [Young-woo] Wait…

35:17.907 --> 35:19.951
- [employee 1] What?
- [employee 2] What's going on?

35:20.034 --> 35:22.453
- [Young-woo] Let… Let's go.
- [employee 1] What?

35:22.537 --> 35:24.413
[employee 2] Look at this heart.

35:24.497 --> 35:27.250
[employee 3] I didn't know
he'd prepare lunchboxes for us.

35:27.333 --> 35:28.835
[quirky music resumes]

35:39.345 --> 35:40.680
[music ends]

35:50.731 --> 35:51.899
[Won-bin] Is this seat taken?

35:58.489 --> 35:59.365
Do you want one?

36:01.033 --> 36:02.368
[footsteps approaching]

36:07.039 --> 36:08.416
[quirky music playing]

36:09.584 --> 36:10.418
[Sa-eon] I get…

36:11.544 --> 36:12.962
carsick.

36:14.046 --> 36:17.258
Doesn't it get worse
if you sit in the back?

36:17.884 --> 36:20.428
Right. Then why don't you sit there?

36:21.929 --> 36:24.974
I think I'll leave my things here.

36:25.057 --> 36:25.892
I see.

36:26.893 --> 36:28.686
Then would you like to sit here?

36:31.147 --> 36:31.981
Thank you.

36:32.064 --> 36:32.982
[Won-bin chuckles]

36:39.989 --> 36:40.990
Coffee…

36:41.991 --> 36:44.076
isn't good on an empty stomach, Ms. Hong.

36:51.667 --> 36:52.543
[You-ri] Proof?

36:53.794 --> 36:56.255
Are we cops or something?
How can we find proof?

36:57.548 --> 36:58.549
A witness?

37:01.177 --> 37:03.137
There's no proof.
How would we find a witness?

37:03.846 --> 37:06.349
Not to mention,
these kids don't have a family.

37:07.516 --> 37:08.726
It's in the development stage.

37:08.809 --> 37:10.394
- If we keep digging…
- [call disconnects]

37:11.103 --> 37:12.897
Hello?

37:12.980 --> 37:14.065
Mr. Han?

37:15.775 --> 37:16.692
What?

37:16.776 --> 37:18.194
He just hung up on me.

37:19.195 --> 37:20.404
Do they want to toss it?

37:21.364 --> 37:23.824
- Well…
- "If the NeoTuber's story is fake,

37:23.908 --> 37:25.243
will you take responsibility?"

37:25.326 --> 37:26.994
Why would I take responsibility?

37:27.078 --> 37:27.954
You have to.

37:28.037 --> 37:29.080
[Sang-woo scoffs]

37:29.914 --> 37:31.707
Why are you helping so enthusiastically?

37:32.333 --> 37:33.376
Because…

37:34.752 --> 37:35.962
[gasps]

37:37.088 --> 37:38.464
Why are you buying so much?

37:39.423 --> 37:40.299
It's not that much.

37:41.175 --> 37:44.178
At least for hungry little ones
whose stomachs can never be filled.

37:45.638 --> 37:47.723
- [all exclaiming]
- [child 1] I'm a huge fan of hers!

37:47.807 --> 37:49.392
[child 2] I need to get her autograph.

37:50.726 --> 37:51.727
I don't believe it.

37:51.811 --> 37:53.813
Thank you so much.

37:54.522 --> 37:56.857
- Hello!
- [child 3] Cool.

37:58.109 --> 37:59.694
Thank you.

38:01.153 --> 38:02.113
[child 4] Wow.

38:02.196 --> 38:04.615
Are you Dr. Sang-woo's girlfriend?

38:05.116 --> 38:07.702
- What?
- [child 5] Want to see his dark past?

38:07.785 --> 38:10.371
If you still like him after,
it's real love.

38:10.454 --> 38:13.541
No, wait.
I'm not Dr. Sang-woo's girlfriend.

38:14.292 --> 38:16.711
[children laughing]

38:22.174 --> 38:23.009
[giggles]

38:28.222 --> 38:30.308
[Sang-woo] Guys, let's eat!

38:30.391 --> 38:31.517
[children exclaiming]

38:33.728 --> 38:34.729
Be careful.

38:34.812 --> 38:36.480
Be careful.

38:36.564 --> 38:38.232
[all laughing]

38:39.150 --> 38:40.526
[children squealing]

38:41.235 --> 38:42.570
[Sang-woo] Let's eat.

38:43.654 --> 38:45.072
[You-ri] No, you can't look!

38:45.156 --> 38:46.532
[Sang-woo] Wait! Hey!

38:46.615 --> 38:48.951
Hey! This isn't right.

38:50.286 --> 38:51.329
[You-ri laughs]

38:56.834 --> 38:57.668
This picture…

38:59.754 --> 39:04.133
I heard the kids started disappearing
around this time.

39:04.216 --> 39:05.926
[You-ri] This was before you came here.

39:06.886 --> 39:08.095
Do you know anything?

39:08.804 --> 39:10.389
No, I don't.

39:10.473 --> 39:13.059
Did any of the birth parents come back
later on?

39:17.980 --> 39:22.360
So the missing kids
had no family searching for them

39:24.570 --> 39:27.198
and no one to remember them all this time.

39:30.785 --> 39:34.705
Shin Yeong-seok liked to play marbles,
and he was so competitive.

39:36.248 --> 39:38.626
Lee Jin-yeong liked cars.

39:38.709 --> 39:40.961
Park Min-woo. He was so…

39:42.588 --> 39:43.589
Such a troublemaker.

39:44.840 --> 39:45.758
I remember them.

39:48.219 --> 39:49.053
These three.

39:51.722 --> 39:52.723
That's strange.

39:53.557 --> 39:54.725
I heard

39:55.476 --> 39:57.978
that four kids disappeared.

39:58.062 --> 39:59.522
There's one more?

40:00.022 --> 40:01.816
Yes, here.

40:06.404 --> 40:08.030
One of the twin brothers.

40:08.114 --> 40:10.116
[eerie music playing]

40:28.259 --> 40:29.427
[phone beeps]

40:36.517 --> 40:39.103
CHANGE OF PLAN. TODAY'S D-DAY.

40:42.648 --> 40:44.650
[eerie music intensifies]

40:50.322 --> 40:51.282
[music ends]

40:51.365 --> 40:52.366
[camera shutter clicks]

41:02.960 --> 41:05.546
[indistinct conversation]

41:08.007 --> 41:09.008
[camera shutter clicks]

41:14.054 --> 41:16.056
[gentle music playing]

41:18.058 --> 41:19.185
[heart beating]

41:22.313 --> 41:23.439
[heart beating]

41:27.234 --> 41:28.235
[heart beating]

41:31.197 --> 41:33.199
[gentle music continues playing]

41:58.641 --> 41:59.850
[sighs]

42:33.175 --> 42:34.134
[music fades]

42:36.178 --> 42:37.429
[phone ringing loudly]

42:40.516 --> 42:41.850
[Young-woo] Hey, honey.

42:43.185 --> 42:44.144
No, I wasn't sleeping.

42:44.228 --> 42:46.397
Is it hard on your own?
Sorry, I couldn't go.

42:48.023 --> 42:48.857
What?

42:52.403 --> 42:53.237
Yeah.

42:54.863 --> 42:57.157
I love you,
my ultimate love in the universe!

42:57.241 --> 42:58.993
Park Eun-yeong, I love you so much!

42:59.076 --> 43:01.662
- [blows dramatic kiss]
- [call disconnects]

43:02.746 --> 43:03.581
[sighs]

43:04.331 --> 43:05.499
[quirky music playing]

43:10.129 --> 43:11.130
I apologize.

43:21.932 --> 43:23.934
[Sa-eon] How do you do that?

43:24.018 --> 43:24.852
Excuse me?

43:26.103 --> 43:27.688
What you just did.

43:28.731 --> 43:30.941
"I love you,
ultimate love in the universe."

43:31.025 --> 43:32.109
You're good at that.

43:32.192 --> 43:33.027
You know,

43:33.819 --> 43:36.405
it's only hard at first,
but it gets easier to do.

43:36.488 --> 43:40.743
Think of it as adding a little flavor
to the affection you usually show.

43:40.826 --> 43:42.077
Say it with a kiss.

43:45.789 --> 43:46.790
Wait,

43:48.459 --> 43:49.960
you do show affection, right?

43:56.383 --> 43:58.302
You've been married for about…

43:58.385 --> 43:59.219
Three years.

44:00.721 --> 44:02.640
You're practically newlyweds. So why?

44:05.684 --> 44:08.437
You know, time sure does fly.

44:08.520 --> 44:11.690
It feels like I got married yesterday,
but it's already been ten years.

44:12.399 --> 44:14.568
Time flies by so quickly.

44:15.194 --> 44:16.612
What's the use of saving it?

44:17.738 --> 44:20.491
When she's by your side,
tell her you love her

44:21.325 --> 44:22.326
and thank her

44:23.452 --> 44:24.536
as much as you can.

44:41.970 --> 44:44.431
[Young-woo exclaiming]

44:44.515 --> 44:47.810
[clears throat] We've unpacked
and warmed up now.

44:47.893 --> 44:49.937
Thank you for the lunchboxes, Mr. Paik!

44:50.020 --> 44:50.854
Thank you.

44:50.938 --> 44:53.941
Now that we're full,
shall we start the sports competition?

44:54.024 --> 44:54.983
[employee 1] Gosh.

44:55.067 --> 44:57.236
Someone stop Mr. Kang.

44:57.319 --> 45:00.072
[employee 2] Yeah.
Who knew he was so into events?

45:00.155 --> 45:03.409
[Young-woo] All events
will be played in pairs.

45:03.492 --> 45:06.495
The teams will be
the spokespersons versus the interpreters.

45:06.578 --> 45:08.288
Let's team up, Hee-joo.

45:09.248 --> 45:10.541
[Sa-eon] No.

45:10.624 --> 45:14.044
We came to build a rapport
with the interpreters.

45:14.128 --> 45:17.423
What's the point of this retreat
if you arrange the teams like that?

45:17.506 --> 45:19.550
Shall we mix them, perhaps?

45:19.633 --> 45:22.344
Mr. Paik, why don't you pick
one of the interpreters first…

45:22.428 --> 45:23.637
Okay.

45:29.518 --> 45:31.520
Let's team up, Ms. Hong.

45:31.603 --> 45:34.273
Then, that's one team!

45:34.356 --> 45:38.068
- Wow. Everyone else can team up too.
- Good luck.

45:38.777 --> 45:40.028
What's the prize?

45:40.112 --> 45:41.405
Ah. [chuckles]

45:41.488 --> 45:43.532
- The winning team--
- Let them pick.

45:43.615 --> 45:46.743
- Excuse me?
- The winning team can pick their prize.

45:47.494 --> 45:48.328
Let's start.

45:49.663 --> 45:50.581
What they want!

45:51.248 --> 45:52.332
Warm up.

46:00.424 --> 46:02.676
The first event is just a warm-up.

46:02.759 --> 46:05.262
We'll start with
a two-person jump rope challenge!

46:05.345 --> 46:06.763
- [all exclaiming]
- [Young-woo] Now.

46:06.847 --> 46:10.726
There's a lot of room for mistakes
in this event, so you'll get two chances.

46:10.809 --> 46:13.854
We'll start with Park Do-jae
and Kim Tae-kyeong.

46:13.937 --> 46:15.397
- Spin it.
- [employee 2] Good luck.

46:20.944 --> 46:21.778
[Do-jae] Here I go.

46:21.862 --> 46:23.614
[Young-woo] That was good. That's good!

46:23.697 --> 46:25.282
Nice!

46:25.365 --> 46:28.118
I'll go in first.
Make sure to time it right and jump.

46:28.202 --> 46:30.996
Speed, reflexes, timing, and focus
are all important.

46:31.079 --> 46:34.124
- [Young-woo] Mr. Park, you look so calm.
- [people counting] Seven, eight!

46:34.208 --> 46:35.709
[Young-woo] That's too bad.

46:35.792 --> 46:36.627
How many?

46:36.710 --> 46:38.629
That makes it seven.

46:38.712 --> 46:40.130
- [Young-woo] Now, next.
- Good job.

46:40.214 --> 46:41.840
Okay, next. Mr. Paik's team.

46:45.594 --> 46:47.137
- [employee 3] Come on.
- [Sa-eon grunts]

46:50.641 --> 46:51.558
[employee 3] One.

46:52.351 --> 46:53.560
[Young-woo] Are you okay?

46:53.644 --> 46:55.729
- Take it easy.
- That's zero.

46:56.563 --> 46:57.606
Mr. Paik, you're out!

46:59.900 --> 47:01.026
I'm sorry.

47:01.109 --> 47:03.111
[quirky music playing]

47:05.322 --> 47:07.491
[Young-woo] Once again. Next.
[clears throat]

47:07.574 --> 47:08.951
It's smooth this time.

47:09.034 --> 47:10.744
Now.

47:10.827 --> 47:12.454
I've figured out the trick.

47:12.538 --> 47:13.914
I can do a good job this time.

47:13.997 --> 47:16.875
Once I find the rhythm after a few jumps,
then you can--

47:17.501 --> 47:18.418
Are you listening?

47:18.502 --> 47:20.420
[Hee-joo] I'll go first. Just follow me.

47:21.046 --> 47:22.673
[people counting] Twelve.

47:22.756 --> 47:24.174
[Young-woo] How many was that?

47:24.258 --> 47:26.009
- It's 12 this time.
- [Young-woo] Okay.

47:26.093 --> 47:28.220
Okay, let's get Mr. Paik's team.
Team Paik?

47:35.519 --> 47:37.062
- Now!
- [employee 3] There you go! Okay!

47:39.064 --> 47:40.315
[all exclaiming]

47:41.066 --> 47:43.026
- You have to go.
- [Young-woo] Go, Mr. Paik!

47:43.110 --> 47:45.153
We'll count once Mr. Paik comes in.

47:47.239 --> 47:48.073
[grunts softly]

47:48.156 --> 47:49.700
[clapping]

47:59.876 --> 48:01.878
[pleasant music playing]

48:14.891 --> 48:15.851
[music ends]

48:20.314 --> 48:22.232
We finally found one.

48:22.316 --> 48:23.442
The victim's family.

48:24.109 --> 48:28.071
If his little brother is alive
and if he was looking for his brother,

48:29.072 --> 48:31.074
then he may know something.

48:31.992 --> 48:33.160
I know.

48:33.243 --> 48:34.578
But…

48:34.661 --> 48:37.789
it won't be easy to figure out
where he is or how he's living.

48:37.873 --> 48:41.793
Well, the director said that
the old documents were lost or discarded

48:41.877 --> 48:43.420
when the operating foundation changed.

48:43.503 --> 48:44.379
[Sang-woo] For now,

48:44.463 --> 48:47.716
I'll ask the kids from the orphanage
I can get in touch with.

48:47.799 --> 48:51.053
[exclaims] That's a great idea.

48:51.803 --> 48:53.013
[both chuckle]

48:56.141 --> 48:58.143
[soft, energetic music playing]

49:01.229 --> 49:03.482
[Young-woo] It's the finals
for the three-legged race.

49:03.565 --> 49:05.484
Mr. Paik and Hong Hee-joo

49:05.567 --> 49:07.944
versus Jeong Won-bin and Ahn Jin-hee.

49:08.028 --> 49:11.114
Who will be the winning team?

49:15.035 --> 49:17.663
- [gun fires]
- [Young-woo] And they're off! Team Paik!

49:17.746 --> 49:20.582
They're running neck-and-neck!

49:20.666 --> 49:22.959
- Be careful!
- [employee 1] Go, Mr. Paik!

49:23.043 --> 49:24.127
Anyone, just win!

49:24.211 --> 49:26.546
- Good luck!
- That's a three-legged race!

49:26.630 --> 49:29.675
Won-bin's team is slowing down!
The finish line is just ahead!

49:29.758 --> 49:31.843
And they're down! Team Paik!

49:35.347 --> 49:37.015
[pleasant music playing]

49:39.893 --> 49:41.186
Team Paik wins!

49:41.269 --> 49:43.647
- Paik Sa-eon! Hong Hee-joo!
- [all cheering]

49:43.730 --> 49:46.900
- [all cheering] Paik Sa-eon! Hong Hee-joo!
- [Young-woo] Paik Sa-eon!

49:46.983 --> 49:48.026
[Sa-eon laughs]

49:59.204 --> 50:00.038
[Sa-eon] Ah.

50:00.664 --> 50:02.624
I'm sorry. I got carried away.

50:05.585 --> 50:06.420
[Young-woo] Okay.

50:07.254 --> 50:08.422
Anyway, congrats!

50:08.505 --> 50:10.841
What prize should we prepare
for the winning team?

50:10.924 --> 50:12.467
Tell me if you want something.

50:12.551 --> 50:14.886
There is something I want.

50:17.514 --> 50:21.435
[Young-woo] The weather's nice.
The angle's nice.

50:21.518 --> 50:22.602
And the models…

50:23.687 --> 50:26.481
Did you two fight already?

50:26.565 --> 50:28.775
Can you move closer together?

50:29.735 --> 50:31.820
Yes, that's good.

50:32.654 --> 50:35.574
But is one photo really enough?

50:35.657 --> 50:37.576
I mean, it's your first-place prize.

50:37.659 --> 50:39.536
There's meat and rice.

50:39.619 --> 50:40.704
I don't need it.

50:41.538 --> 50:43.874
A souvenir photo will be enough.

50:44.541 --> 50:46.251
[Young-woo] Okay, then.

50:47.085 --> 50:47.919
Now.

50:48.003 --> 50:49.087
Smile.

50:50.922 --> 50:52.257
Bigger!

50:55.218 --> 50:56.136
That's good.

50:56.219 --> 50:58.305
Now… Tilt your head.

50:59.014 --> 51:00.766
Tilt. No, towards the middle, Mr. Paik.

51:00.849 --> 51:03.351
There you go. That's good. That's perfect!

51:03.435 --> 51:04.936
Good. Don't move.

51:05.479 --> 51:06.396
Make a hand heart.

51:06.480 --> 51:08.899
[pleasant music continues playing]

51:33.590 --> 51:34.508
That's great.

51:35.550 --> 51:36.384
Now.

51:36.468 --> 51:37.511
I'll take it now.

51:37.594 --> 51:38.428
Good.

51:38.512 --> 51:39.930
[in English] Smile!

51:46.394 --> 51:47.604
[music ends]

51:48.980 --> 51:50.232
[people panting]

51:52.567 --> 51:53.693
[Young-woo in Korean] Wait.

51:53.777 --> 51:54.861
Let's rest.

51:55.654 --> 51:57.364
Let's rest for a little.

51:57.447 --> 51:59.449
But you're dressed for the Himalayas.

52:00.283 --> 52:01.451
[Jin-hee] Yeah.

52:01.535 --> 52:03.829
Why did you want to hike this mountain?

52:03.912 --> 52:05.831
[panting] Did I suggest it? Did I?

52:06.581 --> 52:09.167
That man flying up there did.

52:10.168 --> 52:11.670
Wow, well…

52:11.753 --> 52:14.089
Can you believe Hong Hee-joo's stamina?

52:14.172 --> 52:15.257
It's unexpected.

52:15.340 --> 52:16.925
It's not just her stamina.

52:17.008 --> 52:19.427
Don't those two have good chemistry?

52:19.511 --> 52:20.554
I felt it too.

52:20.637 --> 52:21.847
During the three-legged race,

52:21.930 --> 52:23.014
- they were so in sync.
- Yes!

52:23.098 --> 52:24.391
He's a married man!

52:24.474 --> 52:25.725
You scared me!

52:25.809 --> 52:27.978
You said it before too.

52:28.061 --> 52:31.439
That sparks flew between the two
on the day of the interview.

52:31.523 --> 52:32.732
- When did I?
- Goodness.

52:32.816 --> 52:35.735
That's enough nonsense. Help me up.

52:35.819 --> 52:36.653
[employee grunts]

52:36.736 --> 52:38.613
[Young-woo] Here. One, two!

52:38.697 --> 52:39.865
[groans]

52:39.948 --> 52:41.074
[breathing heavily]

52:52.669 --> 52:54.671
[soft music playing]

53:13.565 --> 53:15.483
[panting]

53:17.235 --> 53:18.987
[panting]

53:19.070 --> 53:20.363
[breathing heavily]

53:25.535 --> 53:26.912
Is that shirt all you have?

53:46.306 --> 53:48.016
It's cold once the sweat dries.

53:48.099 --> 53:49.392
Wear it later.

53:52.938 --> 53:54.022
[exhales]

53:56.441 --> 53:58.526
[employee] Where'd you buy
your hiking clothes?

53:58.610 --> 54:00.695
- [Young-woo] That's not the issue.
- [chattering]

54:00.779 --> 54:03.281
- [employee 1] You dressed up the most.
- [employee 2] Over here.

54:03.949 --> 54:07.077
- [Young-woo] Who's the youngest among us?
- [Won-bin] Me. I am.

54:14.209 --> 54:16.211
[pleasant music playing]

54:20.757 --> 54:21.758
[panting]

54:25.178 --> 54:26.513
[woman] It's so pretty.

54:40.860 --> 54:42.779
We're here.

54:46.908 --> 54:47.951
[Jin-hee] It's beautiful.

54:48.034 --> 54:49.369
[camera shutters clicking]

54:50.662 --> 54:51.496
[Jin-hee] Hee-joo.

54:51.579 --> 54:53.206
Shall we take a photo together?

54:53.289 --> 54:54.457
- Yeah.
- [Jin-hee] Sounds good.

54:57.252 --> 54:59.254
One, two, three.

54:59.838 --> 55:01.423
- [camera shutter clicks]
- [chuckling]

55:01.506 --> 55:04.050
Great job, everyone.

55:04.134 --> 55:06.386
Come and gather. Let's take a group photo.

55:06.469 --> 55:07.887
Here's the banner.

55:08.722 --> 55:10.015
Hold that up.

55:10.598 --> 55:11.725
Rows of two?

55:13.935 --> 55:14.769
Okay, behind.

55:14.853 --> 55:16.187
Don't push in the back.

55:16.271 --> 55:18.982
You'll be gone for good
if you fall, got it?

55:19.607 --> 55:20.442
Now.

55:20.525 --> 55:22.610
Okay, that's good. Gather together.

55:25.447 --> 55:26.614
[people chuckle]

55:26.698 --> 55:28.241
[Young-woo] Get closer.

55:28.324 --> 55:30.410
- [employee] Closer.
- [Young-woo] Okay, that's good.

55:30.493 --> 55:31.453
[woman 1] Look at that.

55:31.536 --> 55:33.872
Isn't that Spokesperson Paik Sa-eon?

55:33.955 --> 55:36.207
- [Young-woo] That's right.
- [woman 2] It is him!

55:36.291 --> 55:39.252
- [Young-woo] Let us take a photo.
- [woman 2] You're so handsome!

55:39.335 --> 55:40.378
[Young-woo] Just a moment.

55:40.462 --> 55:42.756
- Can we take a photo with you?
- [Young-woo] After ours.

55:42.839 --> 55:44.382
Wait a moment.

55:44.466 --> 55:47.218
- Just a moment. Please, don't push.
- [all clamoring]

55:47.302 --> 55:48.762
[Young-woo] Please maintain order.

55:49.304 --> 55:50.305
Just a moment.

55:51.222 --> 55:52.182
Mr. Park.

55:52.265 --> 55:55.185
People, please don't push. Maintain order.

55:56.144 --> 55:56.978
Mr. Park! Mr. Paik!

55:57.062 --> 55:58.480
[people clamoring]

56:03.276 --> 56:05.528
- [employee screaming]
- Excuse me!

56:05.612 --> 56:07.530
[gasping] Oh no!

56:07.614 --> 56:09.365
- [crying] What do we do?
- What is it?

56:09.449 --> 56:11.201
A person fell.

56:11.868 --> 56:13.369
- Who?
- [Won-bin] Hong Hee-joo.

56:13.453 --> 56:15.663
It happened in the blink of an eye.
Down the cliff.

56:16.289 --> 56:17.957
[Young-woo] Step back. Please, step back.

56:18.041 --> 56:18.958
Hong Hee-joo.

56:19.584 --> 56:21.252
Hong Hee-joo!

56:23.546 --> 56:25.006
[suspenseful music playing]

56:25.673 --> 56:26.674
[exhales heavily]

56:44.484 --> 56:46.820
[Young-woo] We were just about to take
a group photo,

56:47.570 --> 56:49.155
and some hikers approached us.

56:49.239 --> 56:51.741
They barged in and started pushing.

56:51.825 --> 56:53.368
First, deploy the rescue team.

56:54.160 --> 56:56.412
It's almost 6 p.m.
It'll be bad if it gets dark.

56:56.496 --> 56:57.330
Mr. Paik!

57:08.675 --> 57:10.176
[rescuer] How did he come from there?

57:10.260 --> 57:12.095
He went down before you got here.

57:12.178 --> 57:14.264
- Down there?
- Are you okay? Were you hurt?

57:14.347 --> 57:16.516
How could you go down there like that?

57:16.599 --> 57:19.185
I saw a broken tree. [breathing heavily]

57:19.269 --> 57:21.563
I think she hit that on her way down.

57:21.646 --> 57:23.648
Can we deploy the rescue dogs right away?

57:23.731 --> 57:26.693
Yes, but we don't have
the missing person's belongings.

57:29.362 --> 57:31.114
[Sa-eon] They can smell this.

57:31.197 --> 57:33.575
She has my jacket around her waist. Hurry.

57:35.493 --> 57:37.162
Did you get through?

57:37.245 --> 57:38.246
No, I can't get through.

57:38.329 --> 57:39.456
[sighs]

57:41.499 --> 57:43.501
[suspenseful music continues playing]

57:44.669 --> 57:45.753
HONG HEE-JOO

57:50.008 --> 57:52.051
[automated voice]
The number you have dialed is…

57:53.511 --> 57:54.345
[Sa-eon sighs]

57:55.680 --> 57:58.391
[automated voice]
The number you have dialed is…

57:58.475 --> 58:00.143
[breathes heavily]

58:43.770 --> 58:44.687
[music stops]

58:55.240 --> 58:56.241
[gasps]

58:56.324 --> 58:57.367
[groans]

59:03.081 --> 59:04.165
[groaning]

59:11.130 --> 59:12.215
[breathing heavily]

59:16.010 --> 59:18.012
[Young-woo] Mr. Paik. Over here.

59:19.180 --> 59:22.141
[Young-woo] People, please don't push.
Maintain order.

59:26.271 --> 59:27.146
Someone…

59:31.192 --> 59:32.193
[groans]

59:32.860 --> 59:34.487
[breathing heavily]

59:43.913 --> 59:45.081
[groans]

59:45.832 --> 59:47.458
[breathing heavily]

59:53.006 --> 59:54.090
[groans]

59:54.173 --> 59:55.883
[breathing heavily]

01:00:02.765 --> 01:00:03.600
[groans]

01:00:05.893 --> 01:00:07.645
[breathing heavily]

01:00:25.955 --> 01:00:26.873
[line disconnects]

01:00:30.710 --> 01:00:31.544
[kidnapper] Sis?

01:00:32.337 --> 01:00:35.089
Do you know what kind of phone this is?

01:00:35.173 --> 01:00:36.341
This…

01:00:37.300 --> 01:00:39.177
can only call Paik Sa-eon.

01:00:39.260 --> 01:00:40.678
[Hee-joo] That was really true?

01:00:42.597 --> 01:00:44.349
Why is he so meticulous?

01:00:49.896 --> 01:00:50.897
Hong Hee-joo!

01:00:55.735 --> 01:00:57.153
- Hong Hee-joo!
- [phone vibrating]

01:00:58.696 --> 01:00:59.697
PARK DO-JAE

01:01:01.157 --> 01:01:03.660
- What happened?
- [Do-jae] They're still searching.

01:01:03.743 --> 01:01:07.288
They're searching up to 300 meters
downstream of the cliff, but…

01:01:07.372 --> 01:01:08.331
[phone beeping]

01:01:08.414 --> 01:01:09.499
NBN KANG TAE-KYEONG

01:01:10.792 --> 01:01:14.045
Reporters keep calling me.
Has it already spread to the media?

01:01:14.128 --> 01:01:16.714
[Do-jae] I'll regulate it.
And I'll expand the search radius.

01:01:16.798 --> 01:01:18.758
What about the security footage?

01:01:18.841 --> 01:01:21.719
The police are checking the footage
near the trail and summit.

01:01:21.803 --> 01:01:25.098
Our team members and people,
who were nearby when it happened,

01:01:25.181 --> 01:01:26.599
are being questioned as witnesses.

01:01:26.683 --> 01:01:29.143
If you find anything, call me right away.

01:01:31.813 --> 01:01:32.730
[call disconnects]

01:01:32.814 --> 01:01:33.940
[phone vibrating]

01:01:34.440 --> 01:01:35.775
CHUGYEONG DAILY NEWS PARK GUK-JIN

01:01:38.820 --> 01:01:40.279
[rescuer] Are you going to get that?

01:01:41.072 --> 01:01:42.198
No, I'm not.

01:01:44.909 --> 01:01:47.286
Because there's a call I'm waiting for.

01:01:50.373 --> 01:01:51.332
[groaning]

01:01:54.919 --> 01:01:55.837
[exhales heavily]

01:01:59.924 --> 01:02:01.342
[breathing heavily]

01:02:04.262 --> 01:02:06.806
[Hee-joo] Are they conducting a search?

01:02:08.516 --> 01:02:10.268
Why don't I hear anything?

01:02:11.644 --> 01:02:15.565
Shouldn't there be helicopters
and drones looking for me?

01:02:24.365 --> 01:02:25.199
[sighs]

01:02:26.075 --> 01:02:27.660
Is this how I'll get caught?

01:02:30.121 --> 01:02:31.372
I'm being punished.

01:02:32.582 --> 01:02:34.834
I should've confessed earlier.

01:02:36.627 --> 01:02:39.464
Yeah, it's for the best.

01:02:39.547 --> 01:02:41.632
I'll finally say it to him now.

01:02:44.051 --> 01:02:45.052
Yeah.

01:02:46.053 --> 01:02:46.971
Yeah.

01:02:48.639 --> 01:02:50.308
He might not pick up.

01:02:50.391 --> 01:02:51.559
No.

01:02:52.393 --> 01:02:55.313
It's over if he doesn't.
I need to snap out of it!

01:02:55.396 --> 01:02:56.814
Get it together.

01:02:56.898 --> 01:02:58.107
[breathing heavily]

01:03:05.114 --> 01:03:09.952
PAIK SA-EON

01:03:10.453 --> 01:03:12.580
Pick up. No. Don't pick up.

01:03:12.663 --> 01:03:13.664
[line ringing]

01:03:13.748 --> 01:03:15.082
Pick up, please.

01:03:20.630 --> 01:03:21.714
Hong Hee-joo!

01:03:24.258 --> 01:03:25.510
Hong Hee-joo!

01:03:28.012 --> 01:03:29.180
Hong Hee-joo!

01:03:31.474 --> 01:03:32.725
[phone vibrating]

01:03:36.979 --> 01:03:37.939
Hee-joo.

01:03:39.690 --> 01:03:40.525
I mean…

01:03:41.484 --> 01:03:42.318
406.

01:03:43.277 --> 01:03:44.195
What about Hee-joo?

01:03:45.571 --> 01:03:46.739
How is she?

01:03:47.532 --> 01:03:50.785
[Hee-joo] Does he think we're together?

01:03:50.868 --> 01:03:53.371
406, can you hear me?

01:03:56.874 --> 01:03:59.126
You said to call when there's a corpse.

01:04:02.213 --> 01:04:03.714
That's why I called.

01:04:04.715 --> 01:04:05.883
Come take her.

01:04:09.136 --> 01:04:10.137
That's good.

01:04:11.681 --> 01:04:13.182
Thank you for calling me.

01:04:15.309 --> 01:04:16.811
Where did Hee-joo fall?

01:04:17.520 --> 01:04:19.063
Just tell me the location.

01:04:19.146 --> 01:04:20.940
[melancholy music playing]

01:04:25.486 --> 01:04:26.696
[breathing heavily]

01:04:31.242 --> 01:04:32.535
I don't know.

01:04:32.618 --> 01:04:33.536
406!

01:04:34.370 --> 01:04:35.663
Listen to me carefully.

01:04:35.746 --> 01:04:39.166
I've put a first-aid kit
inside of Hee-joo's backpack.

01:04:39.250 --> 01:04:41.794
At the bottom of the kit,
there's a portable flare.

01:04:41.878 --> 01:04:44.171
You can ignite it by striking the top lid.

01:04:44.255 --> 01:04:46.299
I hope Hee-joo finds it and uses it.

01:04:47.758 --> 01:04:49.427
What do you think, 406?

01:04:50.177 --> 01:04:51.304
If Hee-joo wakes up,

01:04:53.014 --> 01:04:54.807
wouldn't she try to search for something?

01:05:02.273 --> 01:05:03.316
[groans]

01:05:03.983 --> 01:05:05.610
[panting]

01:05:06.861 --> 01:05:09.947
[Sa-eon] Are you scared?

01:05:10.031 --> 01:05:11.032
Me?

01:05:12.283 --> 01:05:14.660
What's there to be scared of?

01:05:15.953 --> 01:05:16.787
I'm…

01:05:20.207 --> 01:05:22.126
scared to death right now.

01:05:22.209 --> 01:05:24.003
PAIK SA-EON

01:05:27.465 --> 01:05:29.175
[sobbing]

01:05:44.857 --> 01:05:46.192
[crying]

01:05:52.323 --> 01:05:53.199
[groans]

01:05:55.534 --> 01:05:57.703
[Sa-eon] 406!

01:05:59.330 --> 01:06:00.289
Are you there?

01:06:00.373 --> 01:06:01.374
Answer me!

01:06:01.457 --> 01:06:03.459
[sobbing] I can hear you.

01:06:04.627 --> 01:06:05.628
[sighs in relief]

01:06:10.758 --> 01:06:12.510
The temperature has dropped.

01:06:13.594 --> 01:06:16.347
Do you think Hee-joo's cold?

01:06:17.515 --> 01:06:19.892
I don't know if she's wearing my jacket.

01:06:20.726 --> 01:06:22.520
There's water in her backpack too.

01:06:22.603 --> 01:06:24.438
She can't get dehydrated.

01:06:25.898 --> 01:06:28.359
She needs to drink water. [sobbing]

01:06:31.904 --> 01:06:33.030
[flare gun popping]

01:06:35.366 --> 01:06:37.493
[intense music playing]

01:06:37.576 --> 01:06:38.828
You did it.

01:06:39.578 --> 01:06:40.955
I can see it.

01:06:43.165 --> 01:06:44.375
[sobbing]

01:06:45.418 --> 01:06:47.169
Come quickly.

01:06:47.253 --> 01:06:49.171
[Sa-eon] I'm on my way. Don't hang up!

01:06:49.255 --> 01:06:51.173
And if you can,

01:06:51.757 --> 01:06:53.259
please tell Hee-joo

01:06:53.342 --> 01:06:54.635
not to worry.

01:06:55.219 --> 01:06:57.972
Tell her I'll be right there!

01:06:58.055 --> 01:06:59.724
[sobbing]

01:06:59.807 --> 01:07:01.809
[intense music continues playing]

01:07:15.448 --> 01:07:18.367
WHEN THE PHONE RINGS

01:07:22.705 --> 01:07:23.622
Tell me.

01:07:24.665 --> 01:07:27.334
I'll say it once,
so listen carefully, 406.

01:07:28.169 --> 01:07:29.920
My true feelings for Hee-joo…

01:07:30.004 --> 01:07:32.423
What are your true feelings?

01:07:33.340 --> 01:07:34.508
Tell me.

01:07:40.139 --> 01:07:41.307
I can't hear you.

01:07:45.561 --> 01:07:46.687
[softly] Hong Hee-joo.

01:07:48.689 --> 01:07:49.774
I like you.

01:07:53.194 --> 01:07:55.321
[soft song playing]

01:08:55.923 --> 01:08:58.843
WHEN THE PHONE RINGS

01:08:58.926 --> 01:09:01.178
[Sa-eon] Starting now, I want you
to answer my questions.

01:09:01.262 --> 01:09:03.097
The most important question.

01:09:03.180 --> 01:09:04.098
Did you see his face?

01:09:04.181 --> 01:09:05.224
I like it.

01:09:05.307 --> 01:09:07.309
I like feeling your heartbeat.

01:09:07.852 --> 01:09:10.187
Is he taking a shower? Why?

01:09:10.271 --> 01:09:11.939
[Sa-eon] We've already slept together.

01:09:12.022 --> 01:09:13.232
[You-ri] Is this real?

01:09:13.315 --> 01:09:17.153
[Sa-eon] I felt regretful.
I don't think I've done enough for you.

01:09:17.236 --> 01:09:18.362
No, I mean just me!

01:09:18.445 --> 01:09:20.531
You should return my phone.

01:09:20.614 --> 01:09:21.907
I'm on my way. Open the door.

01:09:21.991 --> 01:09:22.825
[door opens]

01:09:27.413 --> 01:09:29.415
Subtitle translation by: Sue Mounce
